description:
We are looking for high\\-calibre individuals to join the application development team of the Information Technology Department for serving the HKMC Group.

##### **Job Descriptions**

* Analyze, design, and implement complex application systems, focusing on Oracle PL/SQL and Java technologies;
* Conduct system analysis to identify areas for improvement and propose solutions;
* Assist IT Managers on projects and liaise with external vendors and internal teams;
* Contribute to ad hoc projects, user queries, application support, occasional non\\-office hour support and other duties as required; and
* The employment will be on contract basis subject to renewal.

##### **Requirements**

* University degree in IT\\-related disciplines;
* A minimum of 4 years' experiece in system development experience, preferably with experience in banking, risk management or insurance industry;
* Experience or expertise in:
	+ Oracle PL/SQL;
	+ Java technologies (SpringBoot, J2EE/ Jakarta EE);
	+ JavaScript (Vue.js framework experience required; TypeScript a plus);
	+ Reporting Tools (MS SQL Server Reports, Jasper Reports, Crystal Reports);
	+ Quasar UI framework, MyBatis, Nginx, Redis a plus;
	+ Python, Databrick in Azure development a plus;
	+ MS Access VBA, Oracle Forms/Reports a plus;
* Experience in requirement gathering, design, programming, testing and implementation;
* Knowledge of mortgage, loan systems and accounting would be an advantage;
* Excellent problem\\-solving skills and ability to work under pressure;
* Self\\-motived, eager to learn and willing to take up new responsibilities; and
* Good command of written and spoken English and Chinese.

 *(Closing Date: 24 November 2025\\)*

##### **To Apply**


Please quote the position you are seeking and send your application in strict confidence with the application form and a full resume stating your current and expected salary to the Recruitment Officer by either:


Email: \\[email protected]


Postal address: 15/F, Two Harbour Square, 180 Wai Yip Street, Kwun Tong, Kowloon, Hong Kong


Personal data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. Candidates not invited for interview within 8 weeks may consider their application unsuccessful.

**South China Financial Holdings Limited (stock code:** 619\\) has been established more than 37 years and listed on the Main Board of the Stock Exchange of Hong Kong in July 1993\\. We offer a comprehensive suite of financial services, including stock and futures trading, wealth management, investment banking, and asset management, catering to a diverse clientele in Hong Kong and beyond. We are now seeking candidates for Equity Research Analyst positions for the company.



**Responsibility:**  

Conduct detailed, in\\-depth fundamental research on multiple sectors;



Conduct equity research and evaluation for Hong Kong, China market and US equities;



Track and gather news and information from target companies and sectors;



Develop, maintain and update quantitative financial models;



Perform media interview on behalf of company and be the company Spokesperson on various different media platform;



Participate in the company’s investors education activities, including client seminar and other public forums;



Prepare research reports and carry out client presentations.



**Requirement:**  

Bachelor degree in mathematics, finance, accounting, economics or a related field; CFA preferred.



At least 2 years relevant working experience.



Proficiency in spoken and written English and Chinese (including Mandarin).



Analytical skills, attention to details and accuracy.



Sound judgment, decision making, and problem solving skills.



Current SFC Type 1 \\& Type 4 license holder preferable.



We provide attractive remuneration package and prosperous career development to the right candidate. Interested parties please apply with full resume stating current, expected salary and availability via APPLY NOW .

Personal data collected is for recruitment purpose only.



All applications applied through our system will be delivered directly to the advertiser and privacy of personal data of the applicant will be ensured with security.



Full\\-time

**Job Duties:**  

Responsible for day\\-to\\-day execution of IPO and other corporate finance transactions;



Coordinate the works of other professional parties in IPOs and other corporate finance transactions;



Review and comment on all relevant transaction documents;



Assist in project origination including pitch\\-book and proposal preparation;



Perform other job duties as assigned from times to times.



**Job Specification:**  

University degree holder, professionally qualified in accountancy is an advantage;



3 \\- 6 years’ experience in investment banking. Will consider for more senior position with more experience;



Good knowledge about securities market and corporate finance activities;



Good command in English and Chinese. Fluency in Mandarin is a must;



Good PC knowledge (MS Words, Excel \\& PowerPoint);



Able to work under pressure;



Self motivated and a good team player.



All applications applied through our system will be delivered directly to the advertiser and privacy of personal data of the applicant will be ensured with security.



Full\\-time

JOB REFERENCE
**BOCI00890**CONTRACT TYPE
**Permanent**DIVISION
**Investment Banking**JOB FUNCTION
**Debt Capital Markets**The Role



Analyst/Associate, DCM Execution, IBD


Key Accountabilities


* Junior member of DCM team to provide bond service to clients including pitching, deal origination and execution, reporting to the Head of DCM;
* Supporting senior members of the DCM team for pitching and execution work;
* Provide market update to clients and maintain databases;
* Work closely with internal fixed income sales team for marketing and gathering feedback from investors;
* Work closely with DCM Syndicate team on transaction pricing;
* Handle internal reporting and other daily tasks;
* Perform other duties assigned by supervisor from time to time.


Skills \\& Experience


* Bachelor's degree or above in finance, economics, accounting, law or related discipline preferred;
* At least 2 years of relevant experience in DCM obtained within investment banking experience, with offshore DCM work experience is strongly preferred;
* Candidates with full time working experience in Hong Kong or overseas is considered as an advantage;
* Responsible, pleasant and presentable, a good team player;
* Proficient in Microsoft Word, Excel and PowerPoint etc;
* Good ability in written English and Chinese. Fluency in Mandarin and English is mandatory, ability to converse in Cantonese is preferred but not mandatory;


Other Information


* Please apply in strict confidence with full resume, academic record, current and expected salaries;
* The personal data provided will be used for consideration of recruitment only. All personal data of unsuccessful candidate will be destroyed within 24 months;
* Candidates with Enhanced Competency Framework (ECF): please state on the CV.


About BOCI



As a leading investment bank in China and Hong Kong region, the investment banking arm of Bank of China, BOC International Holdings Limited (“BOCI”), is now seeking highly motivated, creative and success\\-oriented professional who would like to pursue the career for supporting our group.

**The Opportunity**
 Join our Core Business Services (CBS) team and you will help support the important business enablement functions that keep our organization running strong. As a CBS professional, you will work across teams to provide the knowledge, resources and tools that help EY deliver exceptional quality service to our clients, win in the marketplace and support EY’s growth and profitability. Major teams within CBS include Finance, Information Technology, Human Resources, Enterprise Support Services, Brand Marketing and Communications, Business Development, Knowledge and Risk Management.




**Overall Position Purpose**
 EY requires a professional who will be responsible to drive and support financial management, as well as to deliver a diverse set of operations projects and activities for the Greater China region. The position will work closely with key members of GC Service Line Leadership team including but not limited to the Service Line Leader, Resourcing Leader, Talent Leader and BD Operations Leader amongst other key internal stakeholders, to ensure successful implementation and execution of operations projects and programs.




**Major Responsibilities:**
* Financial Management Interface
* Monitor, analyze and articulate financial performance issues;
* Initiate short and long terms programs to support the business in addressing structural and/or market issues that are impacting financial performance;
* Financial Planning (short term and long term plan) for the Service Line
* Operational Project Planning, Implementation \\& Support
* Lead the corresponding service line operation team to implement market segment business transformation initiatives, including establishing internal operation system, executing change management tasks, enhancing metrics monitoring/tracking processes, etc.;
* Projects in scope likely to fall within change management, executing and enforcing robust operational and financial controls, and identification of efficiencies;
* Project responsibilities will vary from ‘end to end’ responsibility to project management support to project team member;
* Construct formal project plans, protocols and governance procedures for a range of projects and programs.


**Qualifications, Knowledge \\& Experience**
* Bachelor degree above, 5\\-8 years working experience;
* Experience in working directly with partners and senior executives, and able to influence at all levels and obtain commitments to action;
* Self\\-starter; able to work with limited supervision, to juggle conflicting demands and to prioritize work effectively;
* Extroverted characters and willing to take on challenges;
* Strong organizational skills, attention to detail;
* Proactive, analytical, flexible and confident;
* Candidates with less experience will be considered as Operation Analyst.


**Communication:**
* A committed team player with good interpersonal and communication skills;
* Excellent presentation skill in English and Mandarin (both written and oral) is a must;
* Proficiency in Cantonese is beneficial;
* Overseas education/living experience is considered a plus.


**If you can confidently demonstrate that you meet the criteria above, please contact us as soon as possible.**
**Make your mark.**
**Apply now**

**Overview** 










 With a continued growth in the region, a corporate bank is seeking to hire a
 **AVP, Credit Officer, Corporate Credit** 
 to join the Risk Management department to review and recommend
 **Large corporate credit** 
 transactions

 for approval and maintain a healthy and high credit portfolio for the bank.










**Role Responsibilities** 









* Responsible for day\\-to\\-day management of credit risk arising from exposures booked in Corporate Banking;
* Review and approve credit lending proposals within delegated authority to ensure that the bank’s credit offering is in compliance with bank’s policies, procedures and risk appetite;
* Provide recommendations and highlight key risk issues to front office and Head of Credit;
* Stay on top of high alert to credit worthiness of clients including market situations, provide advice to the related departments on proper credit\\-related actions whenever necessary
* Perform on\\-site credit due diligence by joining joint\\-calls with business unit officers;
* Provide training and guidance to RMs / ARMs on credit policies and processes;
* Prepare portfolio reports / analysis of bank’s credit portfolio;
* Participate in credit policy / new product programme review and ad\\-hoc projects assigned by Management;









**Requirements** 









* University graduate in Finance, Economics, Risk Management or related disciplines;
* Holder of ECF\\-CRM is a plus;
* At least 5 years of relevant experience in commercial / corporate banking with credit assessment experience, broad industry exposure and knowledge of cash flow lending;
* Sound knowledge in various corporate lending products Bachelor degree holder or above, preferably in Finance, Banking or Economics related disciplines
* Independent, attentive to details, good analytical and problem\\-solving skills
* Capability to discuss and guide front offices from early stage of deals to make appropriate credit decision
* Strong analytical, communication and interpersonal skills with good command of both spoken and written English and Chinese









 If you believe you have the relevant skill and experience and is interested in this position, kindly get in touch with Jack Leung with your CV and to engage in a confidential discussion.
